// Course content for K.O. II Coach. Hardware steps follow the official guide: https://teenage.engineering/guides/ep-133/
// Step tuple: [title, press/do, why, what you should hear or see, if stuck, hot controls, layer, options]
// layer (index 6): first = target-rhythm rows revealed (0-4); song = section group (0-5).
// options (index 7, optional): {id: stable step id (never reuse for different content), guide: official guide page slug, os: minimum OS, place: placement-helper row (0 kick, 1 snare, 2 hat, 3 bass)}
// Step text links help topics as: See help: “<exact help[] title>”. (regex /help:? “([^”]+)”/)
const courseInfo={version:'2026.10.13',guideChecked:'2026-10-13',firmware:'OS 2.5'};
const first=[
['Start in an empty project','Press MAIN. If the K.O. II is playing, press PLAY to stop it. Hold MAIN, hold pad 6 as well, then release both: the official guide says “hold main and one of the pads (1-9) to select an empty project”, and projects 6–9 are empty on a new unit. Press PLAY: nothing should sound. Press PLAY again to stop.','An empty project means every note you hear later is one you placed. We will make a one-bar, 90 BPM drum loop, then optionally add bass and a second section. No finger-drumming skill required.','PLAY gives silence, and in MAIN the display shows a position such as 1.1.1.','Projects 1–5 come with factory content. On OS 2.0+ a quick MAIN + number tap can pick a scene instead, so check the display. No empty project? Press SHIFT + MAIN, then select each group A, B, C and D in turn and press SHIFT + A (next empty pattern). If this unit holds music you care about, back it up first with the official EP sample tool. See help: “My project is not empty”.',['MAIN','PLAY','PAD','SHIFT','A'],0,{id:'beat-empty-project',guide:'get-started'}],
['Set the speed and the grid','Press TEMPO and turn X until the display shows 90 (or hold TEMPO and type 9, 0). Press TIMING and turn X until it shows 16, the default 1/16 grid (not 16T). Press − to choose quantize. Leave Y (swing) at no swing. Press MAIN.','The recipe uses ordinary 4/4 and one-bar patterns with 16 steps per bar, four per beat. Quantize snaps live playing to the grid; it matters when you record live in the optional practice at the end. Interval and swing apply when you record, not to notes already written.','At 90 BPM one bar (four beats) lasts about 2.7 seconds.','If you turned Y before, turn it back to no swing. If you changed the time signature before, MAIN + TEMPO opens it; this recipe needs 4/4. Keep the default one-bar pattern length.',['TEMPO','TIMING','X','Y','MINUS','MAIN'],0,{id:'beat-tempo-grid',guide:'functions'}],
['A1: load the kick','Press SOUND, tap A, then tap pad 1. Hold SOUND, type 1 on the pads to load sample 001, and release SOUND. Tap pad 1 to hear it (audition).','Pick a short, low thump, not a long bass note. Factory kicks are stored at 1–99.','Pad 1 makes a low drum sound.','001 is our starting choice, not a guaranteed named sample. If your library differs, use − / + within 1–99 and choose the first short, clean kick you hear. Silent? See help: “A pad is silent”.',['SOUND','A','PAD','MINUS','PLUS'],0,{id:'beat-load-kick',guide:'modes'}],
['A2: load the snare','Stay in SOUND. With group A selected, tap pad 2. Hold SOUND, type 1, 0, 0, release SOUND and tap pad 2.','Choose a crisp snare or clap-like backbeat. Factory snares are stored at 100–199.','Pad 2 sounds sharper and brighter than the kick.','If 100 is unsuitable, browse 100–199 with − / + and pick a short snare. Do not use a long drum loop. See help: “A pad is silent”.',['SOUND','A','PAD','MINUS','PLUS'],0,{id:'beat-load-snare',guide:'modes'}],
['A3: load a closed hi-hat','Still in SOUND with group A, tap pad 3. Hold SOUND, type 2, 0, 0, release SOUND and tap pad 3.','Choose a short “ts” sound. Factory hi-hats are stored at 200–299; avoid a long open cymbal for this first beat.','Pad 3 makes a short, bright tick.','If 200 rings like a long cymbal or your library differs, browse 200–299 for a short closed hat. Your ear decides.',['SOUND','A','PAD','MINUS','PLUS'],0,{id:'beat-load-hat',guide:'modes'}],
['Make the hats quieter','Still in SOUND, tap A3. Turn X down gently until the hat is clearly quieter than the kick. Leave Y alone for now.','In SOUND, X is the selected pad’s amplitude (volume) and Y its pitch. Bright hats can dominate even at a lower level.','Tapping A1 then A3, the hat supports the kick rather than covering it.','There is no magic knob position. Knobs change jobs in different modes, so check you are in SOUND before turning.',['SOUND','A','PAD','X'],0,{id:'beat-hats-quieter',guide:'modes'}],
['Learn the placement move once','Press MAIN and make sure playback is stopped. Hold SHIFT and press − until the display shows 1.1.1. Hold RECORD, tap A1 once, then release RECORD.','This writes the kick at bar 1, beat 1, step 1 (1.1.1). Tapping a pad without RECORD only auditions it; nothing is written.','At 1.1.1 pad A1 lights: a lit pad means a note is written on this step.','Use the display as your guide and keep the loop stopped while placing notes. Made a mistake? SHIFT + B is undo while the umbrella icon is lit. Taps not sticking? See help: “My taps do not repeat”.',['MAIN','SHIFT','MINUS','PLUS','RECORD','PAD'],1,{id:'beat-placement-move',guide:'play-and-record',place:0}],
['Place all four kicks','In stopped MAIN with group A, use − / + to reach each position and hold RECORD + A1 at 1.1.1, 1.2.3, 1.3.1 and 1.4.3. The placement helper below lists them one by one.','These are grid steps 1, 7, 9 and 15: a steady foundation with two off-beat pickups. 1.1.1 is already done; do not add it twice.','A1 lights at each of the four positions, and the kick row matches the target rhythm.','Press PLAY to check, then stop before editing. One wrong note? Go to it and briefly press ERASE + that pad. Holding ERASE + a pad until TRK blinks clears all of that pad’s notes, so keep the press short. See help: “The beat has extra hits”.',['A','MINUS','PLUS','RECORD','PAD','PLAY'],1,{id:'beat-kicks',guide:'play-and-record',place:0}],
['Place the two snares','In stopped MAIN with group A, go to 1.2.1, hold RECORD and tap A2. Repeat at 1.4.1.','These are beats 2 and 4 (grid steps 5 and 13): the backbeat. Count one, TWO, three, FOUR.','A2 lights at 1.2.1 and 1.4.1; the snare lands between the main kicks.','If the display shows a sample number instead of a position, you are still in SOUND: press MAIN. Use group A for both drums. See help: “The snare is in the wrong place”.',['MAIN','A','MINUS','PLUS','RECORD','PAD'],2,{id:'beat-snares',guide:'get-started',place:1}],
['Place the eight hats','In stopped MAIN with group A, hold RECORD + A3 at 1.1.1, 1.1.3, 1.2.1, 1.2.3, 1.3.1, 1.3.3, 1.4.1 and 1.4.3.','These are the .1 and .3 of every beat: eighth notes, counted “1 and 2 and 3 and 4 and” (grid steps 1, 3, 5 … 15). The other eight steps stay empty.','A3 lights at all eight positions, and the hats tick steadily over kick and snare.','Some positions already hold a kick or snare: adding a hat there too is correct. Keep TIMING at 16 so every position exists. The placement helper below lists each one.',['A','MINUS','PLUS','RECORD','PAD','TIMING'],3,{id:'beat-hats',guide:'play-and-record',place:2}],
['Listen to your finished drum beat','Press PLAY on the K.O. II and listen to a few loops. “Hear this recipe” below gives a rough reference. Press PLAY again to stop before editing.','The web sounds are synthesised examples, not your factory samples. Compare the rhythm, not the exact sound.','Kick at 1.1.1, 1.2.3, 1.3.1 and 1.4.3; snare at 1.2.1 and 1.4.1; hats on every .1 and .3. That is a complete drum beat.','Taps that do not repeat were not written: see help “My taps do not repeat”. Extra notes? Press SHIFT + B (undo) while the umbrella is lit, or see help “The beat has extra hits”.',['PLAY','SHIFT','B'],3,{id:'beat-listen-drums',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Tweak the balance, one sound at a time','Press SOUND and tap A1, A2 and A3 in turn. Keep the kick solid, turn the snare’s X down a little if it is harsh, and keep the hats lowest.','This is basic mixing: choosing how loud each part is compared with the others. Keep the original pitch while getting the rhythm right.','Kick and snare are easy to pick out; the hats are supporting detail.','In MAIN, X is input gain, not pad volume: always set pad volume in SOUND. Press MAIN when finished.',['SOUND','A','PAD','X','MAIN'],3,{id:'beat-balance',guide:'modes'}],
['Keep a drums-only section','Stop playback. Hold MAIN and read the scene number on the display; write it down as DRUMS. Release MAIN, then press SHIFT + MAIN once. Hold MAIN again: the number has changed. You are now in a copy.','Commit saves the current patterns as a scene and creates a new scene, so you can add variations without overwriting the previous section. It is not an audio export or a backup file.','The new number differs from DRUMS, and PLAY still gives your drum beat: the copy starts identical.','If you only wanted drums, you can stop here; more layers are optional. Lost track of scenes? See help: “Which scene am I in?”.',['SHIFT','MAIN'],3,{id:'beat-commit-drums',guide:'modes'}],
['Optional: choose one bass sound','Tap B (a short tap selects the group). Press SOUND and tap pad 1 (B1). Hold SOUND, type 4, 0, 0 and release, or browse 400–499 with − / + for a short, low bass. Turn X down if it overwhelms the kick.','Use one pitch only for this first attempt. KEYS (one sample at many pitches) is not needed.','B1 plays one low bass note, separate from the group A drums.','Custom libraries differ. Choose a bass, not a long melodic loop. If it clashes with the drums, try another bass sample or skip this layer. See help: “A pad is silent”.',['B','SOUND','PAD','MINUS','PLUS','X'],3,{id:'beat-bass-sound',guide:'modes'}],
['Place two bass pulses','Press MAIN and make sure playback is stopped, with group B selected. Hold RECORD + B1 at 1.1.1 and at 1.3.1 only.','The bass reinforces beats 1 and 3 (grid steps 1 and 9). The same sample plays at its normal pitch both times.','B1 lights at 1.1.1 and 1.3.1, and the bass row in the target rhythm matches.','If the bass rings over the next note, shorten it in the next step. Do not add a melody until this simple layer works.',['MAIN','B','MINUS','PLUS','RECORD','PAD'],4,{id:'beat-bass-pulses',guide:'play-and-record',place:3}],
['Give the bass a shorter tail if needed','Tap B1, then press SHIFT + SOUND and use − / + to reach the trim page. Leave X (start) alone; turn Y (length) down gently, tapping B1 between changes. Press MAIN when done.','A long bass tail can muddy a small loop. Trim changes how the sound plays in this project only; it does not change the stored file.','The bass pulses sound separate and cleaner.','Never hold SHIFT + SOUND on the trim page unless you mean to crop: that overwrites the sample file and cannot be undone.',['B','PAD','SHIFT','SOUND','MINUS','PLUS','Y'],4,{id:'beat-bass-trim',guide:'modes'}],
['Optional: a little room, not a wash','Press PLAY on the K.O. II. Tap A, then press FX and choose reverb with − / +. Raise the fader only a little: in FX it sets group A’s send. X sets the reverb length; start short.','There is one shared effect; each group chooses how much to send to it. A small amount adds space without blurring the rhythm.','A subtle tail appears behind the drums while their attack stays clear.','Keep the bass send low. Do not hold FX while pressing a group button: that solos the group. Do not hold RECORD while moving the fader unless you want to record automation.',['PLAY','A','FX','MINUS','PLUS','FADER','X'],4,{id:'beat-reverb',guide:'effects'}],
['Turn the loop into a tiny performance','Stop. Hold MAIN, read this scene’s number and write it down as BEAT (drums + bass). Release, then press SHIFT + MAIN once so BEAT stays safe. Now hold MAIN, use − / + to select DRUMS, release and press PLAY. Let it loop four times, switch to BEAT (hold MAIN, − / +) for eight loops, then back to DRUMS for four. Press PLAY to end.','A hand-made intro, main section and outro. You count the loops yourself; chapter 02 teaches song mode, which plays scenes in order automatically (OS 2.0+).','You hear drums only, then drums + bass, then drums only again.','By default a new scene starts the moment you pick it. Optional: press SHIFT + ERASE (system settings), type 4, 1, 1, press ENTER, then press MAIN; scene changes now wait for the end of the bar, so you can pick the next scene a little early. Type 410 the same way to switch back. See help: “Scene changes land at the wrong moment”.',['SHIFT','MAIN','MINUS','PLUS','PLAY'],4,{id:'beat-performance',guide:'modes'}],
['Optional: play along before recording','Hold MAIN, select BEAT and release. Press SHIFT + MAIN once to make a practice copy; BEAT stays untouched. Tap A. Press PLAY and, without touching RECORD, tap pad 2 (snare) once near the end of each loop, just before it starts again. Press PLAY to stop.','So far you placed every note by hand. Live recording is the faster way: you play pads while the loop runs. Practising first costs nothing.','You hear your extra snare while you tap it, and it disappears when you stop tapping.','If your taps keep repeating on their own, RECORD was on: stop and press SHIFT + B (undo) while the umbrella is lit.',['MAIN','SHIFT','A','PAD','PLAY'],4,{id:'beat-live-practice',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Optional: record one live pass with a count-in','Stopped, in the practice copy with group A selected: tap and release RECORD, then press PLAY. After the four-beat count-in, tap A2 once near the end of each loop for two or three loops. Press RECORD to stop recording while the beat keeps playing, and listen.','Quantize (the − you chose in TIMING) snaps each tap to the nearest step, so a slightly early or late tap still lands on the grid. A metronome clicks while you record; TEMPO Y sets its volume.','After you stop recording, the extra snare repeats by itself near the end of every loop.','No count-in? Pressing RECORD and PLAY together starts without one. Nothing recorded? See help: “My taps do not repeat”.',['RECORD','PLAY','A','PAD'],4,{id:'beat-live-record',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Optional: keep it or undo it','Press PLAY to stop. Like the new snare? Keep it. Too messy? Press SHIFT + B while the umbrella icon is lit, then press PLAY to check it is gone. To remove a single note instead, go to it in stopped MAIN and briefly press ERASE + A2.','Undo and erase are your safety net for live recording. Because you recorded in a copy, BEAT is still the clean version.','The practice copy sounds the way you chose. Hold MAIN and select BEAT: it plays without the extra snare.','If undo removes more or less than you expected, this is only a practice copy: select BEAT and make a fresh copy with SHIFT + MAIN. See help: “I erased or changed the wrong thing”.',['PLAY','SHIFT','B','ERASE','PAD'],4,{id:'beat-live-undo',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Your first beat is done','Read the six moves below, then try one from memory without reading this app: in a fresh copy of BEAT (SHIFT + MAIN), move one kick or add one hat. Rebuild your change in the Rhythm lab and listen. Then mark this chapter complete.','Navigate: stopped MAIN, − / + (SHIFT + − / + jumps a bar). Write: hold RECORD + pad. Erase one note: brief ERASE + pad. Undo: SHIFT + B while the umbrella is lit. Commit: SHIFT + MAIN. Select a scene: hold MAIN + − / +.','You can build a drum beat, add bass, perform two sections and fix a mistake. Your scenes so far: DRUMS and BEAT.','To keep your work outside the device, back it up with the official EP sample tool on a computer. This coach cannot capture hardware audio. See help: “How do I export or back up?”.',['MAIN','RECORD','ERASE','SHIFT','PAD'],4,{id:'beat-recap',guide:'get-started'}]
];
const song=[
['Stop and find your beat','Press MAIN. If the K.O. II is playing, press PLAY to stop. Hold MAIN and use − / + until the display shows BEAT, the drums + bass scene you wrote down in chapter 01. Release MAIN. Press PLAY to check you hear drums and bass, then press PLAY to stop.','Your finished beat stays untouched: you build each section in a copy. You will name four scenes in this chapter, BEAT, INTRO, MELODY and BREAK, so keep paper handy.','Playback is stopped and BEAT (drums + bass) is selected.','Skipped the optional bass in chapter 01? Do its two bass steps first. No number written down? Hold MAIN, step through scenes with − / + and play each briefly. Do not press ERASE now. See help: “Which scene am I in?”.',['MAIN','PLAY','MINUS','PLUS'],0,{id:'song-find-beat',guide:'modes'}],
['Make a copy for the intro','With BEAT selected, press SHIFT + MAIN once. Hold MAIN and read the new number on the display; write it down as INTRO.','Commit saves the current scene and creates a new copy, and you are now in that copy. Changes here do not overwrite BEAT.','The INTRO number is different from BEAT.','Commit is not a backup file; it makes a new scene inside this project.',['SHIFT','MAIN'],0,{id:'song-copy-intro',guide:'modes'}],
['Make the intro: remove the bass','In INTRO, tap B once (do not hold it) to select group B. Press MAIN and make sure playback is stopped. Use − / + until the display shows 1.1.1 and briefly press ERASE + B1. Go to 1.3.1 and briefly press ERASE + B1 again.','An intro is smaller than the main beat. A brief ERASE + pad removes only the note on the current step.','At 1.1.1 and 1.3.1 pad B1 no longer lights.','Holding B while pressing − / + switches group B to another pattern instead of selecting it; see help “− and + change the wrong thing”. Erased the wrong note? Press SHIFT + B while the umbrella is lit. Never use ERASE + SOUND: it deletes the sample file. See help: “I erased or changed the wrong thing”.',['B','MAIN','MINUS','PLUS','ERASE','PAD'],0,{id:'song-intro-remove-bass',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Check the intro and your original','Press PLAY, listen to four loops and press PLAY to stop. Then hold MAIN, select BEAT and press PLAY: its bass is still there. Stop.','Copies are independent: changing INTRO did not change BEAT. That is what makes commit safe.','INTRO: kick, snare and hats, no bass. BEAT: drums and bass.','If BEAT lost its bass, you erased in BEAT: press SHIFT + B at once (while the umbrella is lit), or write B1 again at 1.1.1 and 1.3.1 with RECORD + B1. If INTRO still has bass, repeat the previous step in INTRO.',['PLAY','MAIN','MINUS','PLUS'],0,{id:'song-intro-check',guide:'modes'}],
['Make a copy for the melody','BEAT is still selected from the last step. Press SHIFT + MAIN once. Hold MAIN and read the new number; write it down as MELODY.','The melody section starts from BEAT, so it keeps the drums and the bass. INTRO is finished as it is.','Press PLAY in MELODY: drums and bass. Stop.','No bass? You copied INTRO by mistake: hold MAIN, select BEAT, press SHIFT + MAIN again and write the new number as MELODY.',['SHIFT','MAIN','PLAY'],0,{id:'song-copy-melody',guide:'modes'}],
['Choose a melody sound','In MELODY, tap C to select group C. Press SOUND and tap pad C1. Hold SOUND, type 5, 0, 0 on the pads and release SOUND. Tap C1 to hear it.','Group C holds the melody. Factory melodic sounds are stored at 500–599.','C1 plays a melodic sound.','If 500 is silent or unsuitable, browse 500–599 with − / + and choose one short sound you like. See help: “A pad is silent”.',['C','SOUND','PAD','MINUS','PLUS'],1,{id:'song-melody-sound',guide:'modes'}],
['Make the melody quieter','Stay in SOUND with C1 selected. Turn X down until the melody is clearly quieter than the kick and snare.','A melody supports the beat. Too loud, and it covers the drums.','The melody sits behind the drums.','Turn X only in SOUND mode; in MAIN, X is input gain.',['SOUND','C','PAD','X'],1,{id:'song-melody-level',guide:'modes'}],
['Give the melody two bars','Press MAIN and make sure playback is stopped, with group C selected. Hold RECORD, press + once, then release both.','This makes C’s pattern two bars long. A and B stay one bar and simply repeat underneath. Extending adds empty space; it does not copy notes.','The display shows C’s pattern length change from 1 to 2.','Check that C is selected first: each group has its own length. Pressed + twice? Hold RECORD and press − once.',['C','MAIN','RECORD','PLUS'],1,{id:'song-melody-two-bars',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Place melody note 1','In stopped MAIN with group C, hold SHIFT and press − until the display shows 1.1.1. Hold RECORD, tap C1 once, then release RECORD.','The first melody note starts bar 1.','C1 lights at 1.1.1.','Tapping C1 without holding RECORD only auditions it; nothing is written.',['C','MAIN','SHIFT','MINUS','RECORD','PAD'],2,{id:'song-melody-note-1',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Place melody note 2','Use − / + until the display shows 1.2.3. Hold RECORD, tap C1 once, then release RECORD.','The second note lands late in beat 2. Two notes are enough to start.','C1 lights at 1.2.3.','Placed it on the wrong step? Briefly press ERASE + C1 at that exact position.',['C','MAIN','MINUS','PLUS','RECORD','PAD','ERASE'],2,{id:'song-melody-note-2',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Place melody note 3','Use − / + until the display shows 2.1.1 (SHIFT + + jumps a whole bar). Hold RECORD, tap C1 once, then release RECORD.','This starts the second bar with the same melody sound.','C1 lights at 2.1.1.','The display must begin with 2: that means bar 2. If you only ever see 1.x.x, the C pattern is still one bar; repeat “Give the melody two bars”.',['C','MAIN','SHIFT','MINUS','PLUS','RECORD','PAD'],2,{id:'song-melody-note-3',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Place melody note 4','Use − / + until the display shows 2.3.1. Hold RECORD, tap C1 once, then release RECORD.','This finishes a simple four-note shape across two bars.','C1 lights at 2.3.1.','Do not add more notes yet. Listen to these four first.',['C','MAIN','MINUS','PLUS','RECORD','PAD'],2,{id:'song-melody-note-4',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Listen to the melody with the beat','Press PLAY. Listen to two full passes (each pass is two bars). Press PLAY again to stop.','This is your melody section: drums, bass and melody together.','You hear drums, bass and a four-note melody that repeats every two bars.','No bass? You are in a copy of INTRO: hold MAIN and compare the number with MELODY. Melody too busy? Briefly erase the note at 2.3.1 and listen again.',['PLAY','C'],2,{id:'song-melody-listen',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Fit the melody pitch','Press SOUND and tap C1. Turn Y a small amount while tapping C1, and play the beat to compare. Keep the setting that sounds best with the bass.','In SOUND, Y is pitch. A small pitch change can make the melody fit the bass.','The melody sounds comfortable with the kick and bass.','Change Y a little at a time. If nothing fits, choose a different melody sample instead.',['SOUND','C','PAD','Y','PLAY'],2,{id:'song-melody-pitch',guide:'modes'}],
['Make a copy for the breakdown','Stop playback and press MAIN. Press SHIFT + MAIN once. Hold MAIN and read the new number; write it down as BREAK.','MELODY is finished. The breakdown starts as an exact copy of it.','You are in BREAK, and PLAY sounds exactly like MELODY. Stop.','From now on, check the scene number before erasing anything: MELODY must stay as it is.',['SHIFT','MAIN'],3,{id:'song-copy-break',guide:'modes'}],
['Make the breakdown: clear kick and bass','In BREAK, stopped, press MAIN and tap A. Hold ERASE + pad 1 (A1) until TRK blinks on the display, then release. Tap B and do the same with B1.','A breakdown takes the heavy parts away so they hit harder when they return. Holding ERASE + a pad until TRK blinks clears every note of that pad in this pattern in one move.','Press PLAY: melody, snare and hats, but no kick and no bass. Stop.','Hold MAIN first: the number must be BREAK. Wrong notes gone? Press SHIFT + B while the umbrella is lit. A brief ERASE press clears one step only; it is the long hold that clears the whole track. See help: “I erased or changed the wrong thing”.',['MAIN','A','B','ERASE','PAD'],3,{id:'song-break-clear',guide:'play-and-record'}],
['Check all four scenes','Hold MAIN and select INTRO, BEAT, MELODY and BREAK in turn. In each, press PLAY briefly, then stop.','Song mode only plays the scenes you made. If a scene is wrong now, the song will be wrong too.','INTRO: drums only. BEAT: drums and bass. MELODY: drums, bass and melody. BREAK: melody, snare and hats.','If one is wrong, fix it in that scene now. Your paper list of numbers is your map for the next steps. See help: “Which scene am I in?”.',['MAIN','MINUS','PLUS','PLAY'],3,{id:'song-check-scenes',guide:'modes'}],
['Plan the song: one position, one pass','Read the song map on this page. It uses 10 song positions: 1–2 INTRO, 3–4 BEAT, 5–6 MELODY, 7 BREAK, 8–9 MELODY, 10 BREAK.','Each song position plays its scene once, for as long as the scene’s longest pattern. INTRO and BEAT last one bar; MELODY and BREAK last two, because C is two bars long. To make a section longer, give it more positions.','The plan adds up to 16 bars: about 43 seconds at 90 BPM.','Scene numbers and song-position numbers are different things. Keep your paper list of scene numbers beside you.',['MAIN','ENTER'],4,{id:'song-plan',guide:'workflow'}],
['Open the song list and set position 1','Stop playback. Hold MAIN and press ENTER to open the song list editor. A new list starts with one position. Hold SHIFT and press − / + to choose INTRO’s scene number for it.','Song mode plays the positions in order by itself.','Position 1 holds INTRO. You will confirm it by listening at the end.','Song mode needs OS 2.0 or later. Older OS: skip to “Add a little space” and play the sections by hand as in chapter 01’s performance step, following the song map. If this list already holds a song you care about, leave it alone. See help: “The song is too short or has extra positions”.',['MAIN','ENTER','SHIFT','MINUS','PLUS'],4,{id:'song-list-open',guide:'modes',os:'2.0'}],
['Add positions 2–6','Hold SHIFT and press A to add a position, then, still holding SHIFT, use − / + to choose its scene. Do this five times: 2 INTRO, 3 BEAT, 4 BEAT, 5 MELODY, 6 MELODY.','SHIFT + A adds one position; SHIFT + − / + picks the scene for the selected position. Do not assume a new position copies the previous scene: set each one.','Release SHIFT and use − / + to step through the positions: there are exactly six.','Add while you are on the last position. Extra position? Select it and press SHIFT + C to cut it. Wrong scene? Select the position and hold SHIFT + − / +.',['SHIFT','A','MINUS','PLUS'],4,{id:'song-list-first-half',guide:'modes',os:'2.0'}],
['Add positions 7–10','Add four more positions the same way: 7 BREAK, 8 MELODY, 9 MELODY, 10 BREAK. That makes nine SHIFT + A presses in total.','Repeating MELODY gives each melody section four bars; the final BREAK works as a soft ending.','Release SHIFT and step through with − / +: exactly 10 positions, in the order of the song map.','Lost count? Step back to position 1 with − and check each position against the song map. See help: “The song is too short or has extra positions”.',['SHIFT','A','MINUS','PLUS'],4,{id:'song-list-second-half',guide:'modes',os:'2.0'}],
['Play the whole song','Press SHIFT + PLAY to play the song from the start. Listen without touching anything.','This is the moment your separate loops become one song.','INTRO, BEAT, MELODY, BREAK, MELODY, BREAK in that order, about 43 seconds, then it stops by itself.','Much shorter than 43 seconds, or a section is missing: a position is missing or holds the wrong scene. Much longer: a pattern is longer than planned. Keeps looping: song loop is on (system setting 420 turns it off). See help: “The song is too short or has extra positions”.',['SHIFT','PLAY'],5,{id:'song-play',guide:'modes',os:'2.0'}],
['Add a little space','In the song list, press SHIFT + PLAY to start the song. Tap A, press FX and choose reverb with − / +. Raise the fader slightly: that is group A’s send. Tap C and raise its fader a little too. Leave B’s send low.','A little reverb helps drums and melody sound as if they share one room. There is one shared effect; each group only sets how much it sends.','The song sounds more finished, while the kick and bass stay clear.','Change one thing at a time; if it sounds blurry, lower the fader. Do not hold FX while pressing a group button: that solos it. If the song ends, start it again.',['PLAY','A','C','FX','FADER','MINUS','PLUS'],5,{id:'song-reverb',guide:'effects'}],
['Your song is ready to develop','In the song list, play the song once more with SHIFT + PLAY. Then make one change from memory, without reading this app: for example step to the last position with + and add one more BREAK position (SHIFT + A, then SHIFT + − / +). That adds about 5 seconds.','Recap: SHIFT + MAIN commits and moves you into a copy. Hold MAIN + − / + selects a scene. Brief ERASE + pad removes one note; holding ERASE + pad until TRK blinks clears a track. MAIN + ENTER opens the song list; SHIFT + A adds a position; SHIFT + − / + picks its scene; SHIFT + PLAY plays from the start.','Your song has an intro, main groove, melody, breakdown, melody return and ending, and you changed one thing yourself.','Back up the project with the official EP sample tool (computer + USB-C). To record audio, OS 2.5 can send sound over USB to a computer or phone. This app cannot capture your K.O. II. See help: “How do I export or back up?”. Next: chapter 07, the full hip-hop beat.',['PLAY','MAIN','SHIFT','ENTER','A'],5,{id:'song-recap',guide:'workflow'}]
];
// The arrangement chapter 02 builds: [section, scene label, song positions, bars, use]. 10 positions, 16 bars, about 43 s at 90 BPM.
const songMap=[
['Intro','INTRO','1–2',2,'Drums only: kick, snare and hats'],
['Main groove','BEAT','3–4',2,'Your chapter 01 beat: drums and bass'],
['Melody','MELODY','5–6',4,'Drums, bass and the two-bar C melody'],
['Breakdown','BREAK','7',2,'Melody, snare and hats; kick and bass removed'],
['Melody return','MELODY','8–9',4,'Kick and bass come back under the melody'],
['Ending','BREAK','10',2,'The melody without kick and bass, then the song stops']
];
const manual=[
['Samples, notes and patterns','A sample is audio; a pattern is the instructions for when to play it. Sampling your voice does not automatically place it in a beat.','Press SAMPLE to capture a sound, then MAIN to sequence it: stopped, navigate to a position, hold RECORD and tap the pad.','functions'],
['Groups and scenes','A, B, C and D are four groups of 12 pads, each with its own patterns. A scene is the combination of patterns that play together. Suggested roles: A drums, B bass, C melody, D your own samples.','Tap a group to select it. Hold a group with − / + only when you want to change its pattern. Hold MAIN with − / + to choose a scene. SHIFT + MAIN commits: it saves the scene and moves you into a new copy.','modes'],
['Choosing and balancing sounds','SOUND is for choosing a pad’s sample. In this mode X is amplitude (volume) and Y pitch. Factory categories: kick 1–99, snare 100–199, hat 200–299, percussion 300–399, bass 400–499, melodic 500–599.','Select a group and pad, then use − / + (SHIFT + − / + jumps by ten), or hold SOUND and type the number on the pads. Listen to a sound before recording it. Custom libraries may differ.','modes'],
['Live recording without panic','While stopped, tap and release RECORD, then press PLAY for a four-beat count-in. RECORD + PLAY together starts without it. Quantize (TIMING, −) snaps what you play to the grid.','Play your pads after the count-in. Press RECORD to stop recording while playback continues, or PLAY to stop both. SHIFT + B undoes the last change while the umbrella is lit. Practise in a scene copy first.','play-and-record'],
['Precise step recording','In stopped MAIN, − / + moves between positions and SHIFT + − / + moves a whole bar. Hold RECORD and tap a pad to write a note on that step; the pad then lights there. With TIMING at 16 in 4/4, 1.2.3 is grid step 7.','Use the First beat placement helper to see how grid steps match bar.beat.step positions. Do not confuse positions with sample numbers.','play-and-record'],
['Timing, swing and correction','TIMING X sets the note interval (16 = 16 steps per bar); Y sets swing for the 8 and 16 intervals. − chooses quantized recording, + free time. These settings apply when you record, not to notes already written.','For notes already recorded, press SHIFT + TIMING (timing correct), set the interval with X, then, while stopped, press a pad to quantize all of its notes.','functions'],
['Longer loops','New patterns begin at one bar, and each group has its own length. Extending a pattern adds empty bars; it does not copy notes.','Stopped, select the group, hold RECORD and press + to add a bar (− removes one). To double the length and copy the notes, press RECORD to arm, then hold SHIFT and press +. Check the selected group first.','play-and-record'],
['KEYS: one sample, many pitches','Select a sample pad and press KEYS to play that sound across a 12-note keyboard on the pads. Hold KEYS with − / + to choose the octave.','Practise over your drums, stop, then tap RECORD and press PLAY to record with a count-in. On OS 2.5, hold KEYS and turn X for the key and Y for the scale; older versions differ.','play-and-record'],
['Record your own sound','In SAMPLE choose the input (mic, line in and more) with − / +. X is input level and Y threshold. Hold an unused pad, make a short sound, then release.','Tap the pad to audition. Return to MAIN to place it in your beat. If capture never starts, check the source and threshold. USB sampling needs OS 2.5.','functions'],
['Trim and envelope safely','SHIFT + SOUND opens sound edit; − / + chooses a page. On trim, X is start and Y length. On envelope, X is attack and Y release. These edits change the sound in this project only.','Audition small edits. Holding SHIFT + SOUND on the trim page crops the file permanently (OS 2.5); ordinary trimming does not. Holding ERASE + SOUND deletes the sample from the device.','modes'],
['Effects and fader','Groups send to one shared master effect. In FX, − / + selects it and the fader sets the selected group’s send; X and Y depend on the effect.','Reverb: X length, Y colour. Delay: X time, Y feedback. Hold FX + pads during playback for punch-in effects. Holding FX + a group button solos that group. Fader moves recorded with RECORD held become automation.','effects'],
['Automatic song arrangement · OS 2.0+','A song list plays scenes in order. Each position plays its scene once, for as long as the scene’s longest pattern, so repeat a position to make a section longer. It is not an audio export.','Hold MAIN + ENTER to open the list; a new list has one position. SHIFT + A adds a position; SHIFT + − / + picks its scene; − / + moves between positions; SHIFT + C cuts one. PLAY starts at the selected position; SHIFT + PLAY from the start.','modes'],
['Undo and careful erasing','SHIFT + B is undo when the umbrella icon is lit. Erasing notes and deleting a sample file are very different things.','Stopped in MAIN: a brief ERASE + pad removes that pad’s note on the current step. Holding ERASE + pad until TRK blinks removes all of that pad’s notes in the pattern. Holding ERASE + SOUND until SND blinks deletes the sample from the device. Practise on disposable work.','play-and-record'],
['Advanced features · check firmware','Song mode, resampling and hands-free sampling arrived in OS 2.0. USB audio and sample reverse arrived in OS 2.5. This app cannot detect your version.','On OS 2.5 select a sample, press SHIFT + SOUND, press + until TIM and turn X to REV for reverse. Read the official notes before trying resampling or updates.','whats-new'],
['Copy and paste a bar','In MAIN, SHIFT + C copies: press once for the current bar, twice for the whole pattern. SHIFT + D pastes. Useful when a rhythm repeats.','Stopped in MAIN, select the group and go to the bar to copy (SHIFT + − / + jumps a bar). Press SHIFT + C once, move to a bar that already exists in the pattern and press SHIFT + D. Press PLAY to check; SHIFT + B is undo while the umbrella is lit.','play-and-record'],
['Projects, backup and starting fresh','A project is one whole composition; the K.O. II holds nine. On a new unit projects 1–5 come with factory content and 6–9 are empty. Commit copies a scene inside a project; it is not a backup.','Hold MAIN and one of pads 1–9 to change project (on OS 2.0+ a quick MAIN + number tap can pick a scene instead, so check the display). SHIFT + A in MAIN finds the next empty pattern. Back up with the official EP sample tool on a computer over USB-C.','workflow']
];
const controls={MAIN:['Home and arrangement','Navigate and record patterns; hold MAIN with − / + to select scenes. SHIFT + MAIN commits a scene copy. MAIN + ENTER opens the song list (OS 2.0+). MAIN returns here from any page.'],SOUND:['Select a sample','Choose the group and pad first. − / + browses samples; X amplitude, Y pitch. SHIFT + SOUND opens sound edit.'],TEMPO:['Tempo and metronome','X sets BPM; Y the recording metronome volume. Hold TEMPO and type a number for an exact BPM. Our recipe uses 90 BPM.'],TIMING:['Grid and groove','X note interval (16 in this course); Y swing. − quantize; + free time. SHIFT + TIMING corrects notes already recorded.'],SAMPLE:['Capture audio','− / + source, X input level, Y threshold. Hold a pad to capture, release to stop.'],KEYS:['Pitch keyboard','Select one sample, then KEYS. Held KEYS with − / + changes octave. Key/scale shortcuts depend on firmware.'],FX:['Effects','− / + chooses the shared master effect. The fader sets the selected group’s send. Hold FX + pads for punch-in effects; hold FX + a group button to solo that group.'],FADER:['Contextual slider','Normally group level; in FX the group’s send. Hold FADER + a printed pad assignment to choose another parameter.'],X:['Contextual knob','SOUND: amplitude. TEMPO: BPM. TIMING: interval. SAMPLE: input level. MAIN: input gain. Check the mode before turning.'],Y:['Contextual knob','SOUND: pitch. TEMPO: metronome. TIMING: swing. SAMPLE: threshold. Trim page: playback length. MAIN: FX send level.'],MINUS:['− / +','In SOUND: sample choice. In stopped MAIN: positions (SHIFT + − / + moves a bar). Holding a group changes its pattern; holding MAIN changes scene; with RECORD held, pattern length.'],PLUS:['− / +','Same contextual navigation. With RECORD held, adds a bar to the pattern. In the song list, moves between positions.'],SHIFT:['Secondary functions','SHIFT + A next empty pattern; SHIFT + B undo; SHIFT + C copy; SHIFT + D paste; SHIFT + MAIN commit; SHIFT + SOUND sound edit; SHIFT + ERASE system settings.'],ERASE:['Use with care','Stopped in MAIN: brief ERASE + pad removes the note on this step; hold until TRK blinks to clear all that pad’s notes in the pattern. ERASE + SOUND permanently deletes the selected sample.'],RECORD:['Record events','Tap, then PLAY: live recording with a count-in. Hold with a pad: step entry. Hold with +: add a bar. Tap during recording to stop recording but keep playing.'],PLAY:['Start / stop','Starts and stops playback. In the song list, SHIFT + PLAY plays from the start. Stop before position-by-position step entry.'],A:['Group A','A bank of 12 pads with its own patterns. The recipe uses A1 kick, A2 snare and A3 hat. SHIFT + A: next empty pattern in MAIN; adds a position in the song list.'],B:['Group B','Another bank. The recipe uses B1 for bass. SHIFT + B is undo when the umbrella icon is lit.'],C:['Group C','Melody bank in chapter 02, with C1 as the melody sound. SHIFT + C copies (in MAIN: once for the bar, twice for the pattern).'],D:['Group D','Optional bank for your own samples. SHIFT + D pastes what you copied.'],PAD:['Performance pads','Tap to audition; held RECORD + pad writes on a step, and a lit pad has a note on this step. In SAMPLE hold to record audio. In KEYS pads play pitches. With SOUND or TEMPO held they type numbers.'],ENTER:['Confirm / song list','Confirms settings, such as typed system codes. Hold MAIN and press ENTER to open the song list on OS 2.0+.']};
const help=[
['My taps do not repeat','You are auditioning, not sequencing. Stop playback, press MAIN, navigate to the position, then hold RECORD and tap the pad: it lights on that step. For live playing, tap RECORD, then PLAY for a count-in.','play-and-record'],
['A pad is silent','In SOUND select the right group and pad, then browse a sample with − / + and check its amplitude with X. Pads in an empty project have no sound until you load one. In MAIN the fader sets the selected group’s level, so check it is not all the way down.','modes'],
['The beat has extra hits','Press SHIFT + B (undo) while the umbrella icon is lit. Or, stopped in MAIN, go to the unwanted note and briefly press ERASE + its pad. Holding ERASE + pad until TRK blinks clears all of that pad’s notes, so keep the press short. Never use ERASE + SOUND: it deletes the sample file.','play-and-record'],
['The snare is in the wrong place','Our snares sit at 1.2.1 and 1.4.1 (grid steps 5 and 13) with TIMING at 16 in 4/4. Check the display before holding RECORD + A2, and erase a misplaced one with a brief ERASE + A2 at its position.','get-started'],
['My bass loops too soon','Each group has its own pattern length. Select B, stop, and in MAIN hold RECORD and press + to add a bar before writing a longer phrase.','play-and-record'],
['− and + change the wrong thing','Check the mode and what you are holding. SOUND: − / + choose samples. Stopped MAIN: they move between positions. Holding a group: they change that group’s pattern. Holding MAIN: they change scene. Holding RECORD: pattern length. Song list: song positions. Changed a group’s pattern by accident? Hold the group and press the opposite button to go back.','modes'],
['My sample will not start recording','In SAMPLE check the input source (− / +), X input level and Y threshold. A high threshold can stop a quiet sound from starting the capture.','functions'],
['TIMING did not fix old notes','Ordinary TIMING settings apply when you record, not afterwards. For notes already recorded, press SHIFT + TIMING (timing correct), set the interval with X, then, while stopped, press the pad to quantize its notes.','functions'],
['Where did USB or reverse go?','USB audio and sample reverse are OS 2.5 features. Compare your installed firmware with the official notes; this app cannot detect or update it.','whats-new'],
['How do I export or back up?','Commit (SHIFT + MAIN) makes a scene copy inside the project, not a backup. Back up projects with the official EP sample tool (teenage.engineering/apps/ep-sample-tool) on a computer over USB-C; it also transfers samples. To record audio, OS 2.5 can send sound over USB to a computer or phone. The coach has no hardware connection.','functions'],
['My project is not empty','Projects 1–5 come with factory content. Hold MAIN and hold pad 6, 7, 8 or 9 to change project: on a new unit these are empty. On OS 2.0+ a quick MAIN + number tap can pick a scene instead, so check the display. No empty project? Press SHIFT + MAIN to make a scene copy, then select each group A, B, C and D in turn and press SHIFT + A (next empty pattern). Press PLAY: nothing should sound.','get-started'],
['I erased or changed the wrong thing','Press SHIFT + B straight away: undo works while the umbrella icon is lit. If it is not lit, write the notes again from the step text, or go back to an earlier committed scene (hold MAIN + − / +). Keep erase presses short: holding ERASE + pad until TRK blinks clears that pad’s notes, and holding ERASE + a group until PTN blinks clears patterns.','play-and-record'],
['Which scene am I in?','Hold MAIN: the display shows the scene number, and − / + selects another. After SHIFT + MAIN you are in the new copy, and the scene you left keeps the finished version. Write each number and its name (DRUMS, BEAT, INTRO…) on paper as you go.','modes'],
['The song is too short or has extra positions','Each song position plays its scene once, for as long as the scene’s longest pattern. The chapter 02 plan has 10 positions, 16 bars, about 43 seconds at 90 BPM. Open the list (MAIN + ENTER) and count positions with − / +. Extra position: select it and press SHIFT + C. Missing one: SHIFT + A adds a position and SHIFT + − / + picks its scene.','modes'],
['Scene changes land at the wrong moment','By default a scene you pick starts at once (system setting 410). Press SHIFT + ERASE, type 4, 1, 1 and press ENTER so changes wait for the end of the bar (412 waits for the end of the pattern), then press MAIN. Type 410 the same way to switch back. If your OS does not list this setting, switch exactly as the loop restarts and rehearse first.','system']
];
const glossary=[
['Sample','A short audio recording used as an instrument. The K.O. II stores up to 999.'],
['Pad','One of the 12 buttons that play sounds. In many modes they also work as a number pad.'],
['Group','One of four banks (A, B, C, D), each with 12 pads and its own patterns. Tap a group button to select it.'],
['Pattern','The notes one group plays and when. Each group has up to 99 patterns, each up to 99 bars long.'],
['Pattern length','How many bars a pattern lasts before it repeats. New patterns are one bar.'],
['Scene','A saved combination of the four groups’ patterns: one section of a song, such as INTRO or BREAK.'],
['Project','One whole composition. The K.O. II holds nine projects.'],
['Commit','SHIFT + MAIN: saves the current scene and moves you into a new copy of it. Not a backup file.'],
['Song list / song position','In song mode (OS 2.0+), the numbered positions that play scenes in order. Each position plays its scene once.'],
['Song mode','Automatic playback of the song list. Hold MAIN and press ENTER to open its editor.'],
['Beat','The steady pulse you would tap your foot to. Count “one, two, three, four”.'],
['Bar','A group of beats. In 4/4, one bar has four beats.'],
['4/4','The time signature this course uses: four beats per bar.'],
['BPM','Beats per minute: the tempo. At 90 BPM one bar lasts about 2.7 seconds.'],
['Step','One slot in the sequencer grid. With TIMING at 16, a bar has 16 steps, four per beat.'],
['Position (1.2.3)','What the display shows in MAIN: bar . beat . step within the beat. 1.2.3 is bar 1, beat 2, third step (grid step 7).'],
['Subdivision','A smaller slice of a beat. In 1.2.3 the last number is the subdivision.'],
['Note interval (16, 8, 16T)','TIMING X: how many steps a bar has. 16 means 16 steps per bar. T means triplet: 16T has 24 steps per bar.'],
['Quantize','Snapping what you record live to the nearest step. Free time records exactly as you play.'],
['Swing','Delays every second step slightly for a looser, bouncier feel. Works with the 8 and 16 intervals.'],
['Step entry','Placing notes one at a time while stopped: go to a position, hold RECORD and tap a pad.'],
['Live recording','Playing pads while the loop runs and RECORD is on.'],
['Count-in','Four metronome beats before live recording starts: tap RECORD, then press PLAY.'],
['Record arm','RECORD pressed and waiting: the next PLAY starts recording.'],
['Metronome','The click that keeps time while you record. TEMPO Y sets its volume.'],
['Overdub','Recording new notes on top of a pattern that already has notes.'],
['Timing correct','SHIFT + TIMING: snaps notes you already recorded on a pad to the grid.'],
['Audition','Tapping a pad just to hear it. Without RECORD held, nothing is written.'],
['Amplitude (AMP)','The volume of one pad’s sound. X in SOUND mode.'],
['Pitch (PTC)','How high or low a sound plays. Y in SOUND mode.'],
['Sound edit','SHIFT + SOUND: pages for play mode, trim, envelope, time and more for the selected pad.'],
['Pan','Where a sound sits between the left and right speaker.'],
['Trim','Choosing where a sample starts and how long it plays, for this project only. Reversible.'],
['Crop','Permanently cutting the sample file to its trim points (hold SHIFT + SOUND on the trim page). Cannot be undone.'],
['Envelope (attack, release)','How a sound fades in (attack) and how it fades out after you let go (release).'],
['Oneshot','A play mode in which a pad plays the whole sample, one at a time.'],
['Tail','The part of a sound that keeps ringing after the hit. Long tails can blur a beat.'],
['Input level / gain','How loud incoming audio is when sampling. X in SAMPLE mode.'],
['Threshold','In SAMPLE, how loud a sound must be before recording starts. Y in SAMPLE mode.'],
['Line input','The 3.5 mm input for sampling a phone or synth instead of the built-in mic.'],
['Resample','Sampling the K.O. II’s own sound, for example a whole pattern (OS 2.0+).'],
['Hands-free sampling','In SAMPLE, SHIFT + a pad keeps recording without holding the pad; press SAMPLE to stop (OS 2.0+).'],
['Chop','Cutting one sample into slices spread across pads (SHIFT + SAMPLE).'],
['KEYS','A mode that plays one sample at 12 different pitches across the pads.'],
['Scale / key / octave','In KEYS: which notes the pads offer (scale), which note they start from (key) and how high they play (octave).'],
['FX / master effect','The one shared effect (delay, reverb, distortion, chorus, filter or compressor) that every group can send to.'],
['FX send','How much of a group goes into the shared effect. Set with the fader in FX mode.'],
['Reverb','An effect that adds the sound of a room. X sets its length, Y its colour.'],
['Punch-in FX','Temporary effects played by holding FX and pressing pads while the beat runs.'],
['Solo','Hearing one group alone. Holding FX and pressing a group button solos it while playing.'],
['Sidechain','Briefly turning one group down, usually the bass, each time a chosen sound such as the kick plays (OS 2.0+).'],
['Fader','The slider. By default it sets the selected group’s level; in FX it sets that group’s send.'],
['Automation','Fader movement recorded into a pattern, so it replays every loop.'],
['Undo (umbrella)','SHIFT + B undoes the last change. The umbrella icon lights when undo is possible.'],
['TRK / PTN','Display messages while erasing: TRK when ERASE + a pad (stopped) clears every note of that pad in the pattern; PTN when ERASE + a group clears its pattern.'],
['Layer','One part of a beat, such as the kick, hats or bass, added on top of the others.'],
['Loop','A pattern repeating over and over.'],
['Backbeat','Snare on beats 2 and 4, as in this course’s first beat.'],
['Four-on-the-floor','A kick on every beat (1.1.1, 1.2.1, 1.3.1, 1.4.1), typical of house music.'],
['Pickup','A note just before a main beat that leads into it, like the kicks at 1.2.3 and 1.4.3.'],
['Off-beat','A note between the main beats, such as the “and” after a beat (1.1.3).'],
['Eighth notes','Two even notes per beat: count “1 and 2 and…”. With 16 steps per bar they sit on every .1 and .3.'],
['Intro / breakdown / outro','Song sections: the opening, a stripped-back part that makes the next part hit harder, and the ending.'],
['Drop / build','In dance music, the drop is the full-energy part; the build is the rising part just before it.'],
['Groove','The main repeating feel of a track, usually drums plus bass.'],
['Hook','The short, catchy part listeners remember, often a vocal phrase.'],
['Stab','A short, punchy chord or sound hit.'],
['Phrase','A short musical idea, like a sentence in music: a few notes or words that belong together.'],
['Mixing','Setting how loud each part is compared with the others.'],
['System settings','SHIFT + ERASE: device-wide options. Type a code such as 411 and press ENTER to jump to a setting; MAIN leaves.'],
['Firmware (OS)','The K.O. II’s own software version, such as OS 2.5. Some features need a minimum OS.'],
['EP sample tool','teenage engineering’s browser tool for moving samples and backups between the K.O. II and a computer over USB-C.']
];
